WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
Think about this, tech jobs, freelancing and remote work opportunities are booming,

00:06.000 --> 00:09.000
but what if you don't have a laptop or stable internet?

00:09.000 --> 00:14.000
What if you've never learned how to code or navigate digital platforms?

00:14.000 --> 00:17.000
The divide is no longer just about who has technology,

00:17.000 --> 00:21.000
it's about who gets to use it to create a better life.

00:21.000 --> 00:25.000
The digital divide isn't just a developing world issue.

00:25.000 --> 00:28.000
Even in rich countries, the gap is growing.

00:28.000 --> 00:33.000
In the US, millions of rural communities lack reliable broadband.

00:33.000 --> 00:38.000
In major cities, low-income neighborhoods often have fewer public Wi-Fi spots,

00:38.000 --> 00:43.000
outdated computer labs and limited digital literacy programs.

00:43.000 --> 00:46.000
And here's where it gets even more serious,

00:46.000 --> 00:51.000
that digital divide isn't just about convenience, it's about survival.

00:51.000 --> 00:56.000
During the pandemic, people with internet access could work remotely.

00:56.000 --> 01:00.000
Those without it? Many lost their jobs.

01:00.000 --> 01:04.000
Access to healthcare is also shifting online.

01:04.000 --> 01:10.000
Telemedicine, online health portals and digital prescriptions are becoming the norm.

01:10.000 --> 01:16.000
But what about those who can't afford internet or don't know how to use digital healthcare services?

01:16.000 --> 01:21.000
They receive worse medical care simply because they lack access to a screen.

01:21.000 --> 01:24.000
And think about democracy.

01:24.000 --> 01:29.000
Political debates, news updates and even voting are increasingly digital.

01:29.000 --> 01:34.000
When people lack digital access, they're not just disconnected from technology,

01:34.000 --> 01:37.000
they're disconnected from decision-making.

